updates.content_text:
Hey all, it's time for Intermission! This time, we've got a new entry in the Tales from the Constant series of animated shorts, a new login reward, streaming drops, and a skill update beta that you might be interested in.&nbsp;
Tales from the Constant: Birds of a Feather [Animated Short]
You never know who life will place along your path. Some walk with you for a moment, others for a lifetime, yet each leaves something behind.
It's Beta Time!
The WX-78 Skill spotlight will be released to beta later today. This first part of beta is being released a bit&nbsp;earlier than usual so that we have more time to take in feedback and adjust before the scheduled update mid-April. More features of the skill update will release through the beta period. You will also notice that this update focuses on a single character and does not include additional content or features, so that we can focus on making this a great skill update, rather than spreading out resources across multiple tasks. We hope that you agree this focus on quality rather than quantity is the right choice, but this is how we're going to be doing things for a while. More info will come with the roadmap.... soon.&nbsp;
To join us on the beta branch, follow the directions in this post.&nbsp;
Streaming Drops!
The Wriggly Eyebrella has been added to the Chitinous Collection.&nbsp;Check out this post for details.
"Just try to ignore the itching on your scalp."
Login Rewards
To celebrate our recent launch of Rotwood on Steam, we are giving you a nice chest full of cool Rotwood-inspired skins. Simply log in and claim yours!
Klei Rewards
The Bulbin critter has been added to the game as well. Just head over to Klei Rewards page and claim it to unlock it in the game.&nbsp;
Interactive Lore
We've got an interesting update for you today. If you're unfamiliar with our DST interactive lore, head on over to the official Discord or the Interactive Lore section here on the forums.&nbsp;
Up Next
We need some time to work through this beta, and then we'll have a roadmap in early April. We can't put it out yet, for reasons that will be apparent soon. But for now, we hope you all enjoy the beta and interactive lore.&nbsp;

Hello all.
We have made the decision to move the changes from the beta branch over to the main game. It is right before a weekend but we will keep an eye on things in case something does not work quite correct so that we can issue a hotfix for those if they come up. The prior beta branch tested changes made to utility functions and you can read more on that from the beta thread.&nbsp;
